# CompX / Ardor Gaming mice — USB vendor id 25a7.
#
# Two rules for two different jobs:
#
#  * hidraw — the vendor protocol itself (dpi, battery, status, probe, and the
#    EEPROM write behind `rate device --persist`). The config interface is a HID
#    interface that usbhid already owns, and hidraw is how user space reaches it
#    without detaching the kernel driver.
#  * usb_device — optional, and needed only by `rate device --persist
#    --reset-port`: a port reset (USBDEVFS_RESET on /dev/bus/usb/BBB/DDD) that
#    makes the receiver re-enumerate. Nothing else uses it, because the endpoint
#    descriptor does not change with the stored interval, so the re-enumeration
#    costs a second off the bus and shows the same 1 ms. Drop this line if you
#    never pass --reset-port: the hidraw rule above is the whole requirement.
#
# TAG+="uaccess" grants access to the active logind session, so no group
# membership is required on a normal desktop. Without logind (SSH, old
# distros), run the device commands once with sudo instead — do not fall back to
# GROUP="users": device access does not go through that group, membership in it
# is whatever the installer decided, and where nobody is a member the rule
# silently grants nothing. Check with: id -nG
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="25a7", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTRS{idVendor}=="25a7", TAG+="uaccess"
